    "body": "Amazon plans to hire more than 300,000 people across the United States for the holiday season , increasing its hiring target by about 20% from last year as it prepares for the busiest stretch of the shipping calendar.\nWhat’s Related\nThe company said the openings include seasonal, part-time and full-time positions. The hiring covers the fulfillment and transportation work that gets customer orders picked , packed, sorted and delivered during the holiday rush.\nAmazon sought 250,000 workers during last year’s holiday season. This year’s target adds more than 50,000 positions to that total, with new openings scheduled to be posted weekly from October through December.\nSeasonal employees will earn an average of $20 an hour. Amazon also announced expanded health coverage for eligible seasonal workers, although that change will begin January 1, 2027.\nRELATED STORIES: Amazon Adds $1.9 Billion for Delivery Partners and Driver Pay | Amazon Adds Direct Rail Route From Los Angeles to the East Coast\nAmazon to invest $1.5 billion on higher pay\nThe hiring announcement follows Amazon’s September commitment to spend more than $1.5 billion on higher pay for its U.S. fulfillment and transportation employees. That included a $1 hourly increase for eligible workers.\nFull-time employees in those roles now start at a minimum of $20 an hour, with average hourly pay reaching nearly $24. Amazon puts average total compensation above $32 an hour when benefits are included.\nThe company also introduced employee grocery discounts this month. Those include 10% off eligible online grocery and everyday essentials purchases and 20% off purchases at Whole Foods Market stores.\nOther Amazon News\nAmazon Settles D.C. Lawsuit Over Slower Prime Deliveries : Amazon will pay $8.25 million, including refunds to customers, and must disclose future delivery exclusions in the District.\nAmazon Expands Locker Pickup at U.S. Colleges : The expansion gives students more locations to pick up packages at colleges and universities.\nAmazon Delivery Vehicles Got Over 14,000 Citations in NYC : An analysis found thousands of violations, including blocking fire hydrants and speeding in school zones.\nAmazon Plans $100 Million Manufacturing Facility in Indiana : The planned Greenwood facility will produce warehouse robots and create 300 jobs, with operations expected to begin in 2028.",
